{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If a man takes a wife.</b> After speaking of matters of settlement, he spoke of warnings that obligate the indwelling of the Shekhinah in Israel, and to guard against causing its withdrawal through the disqualification of the seed — through forbidden relations, through the admixture of disqualified nations, and through impurity of the camp, as it says: וְהָיָה מַחֲנֶיךָ קָדוֹשׁ וְלֹא יִרְאֶה בְךָ עֶרְוַת דָּבָר וְשָׁב מֵאַחֲרֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 23:15)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:00.291995481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}